# ODS UI (mandatory)

Source of truth: `GEMINI.md` and `ODS_TOKENS_REFERENCE.md`.

## Components

- 100% of UI must use Telekom ODS (`com.telekom.odsystem.*`): `ODSBox`, `ODSColumn`, `ODSRow`, `ODSText`, `ODSIcon`, `ODSImage`, `ODSButton`, etc.
- Never use Compose `Box`, `Column`, `Row`, `Text`, `Icon`, `Button`, or `LazyColumn`.
- Vertical lists and scrollable screens: always `ODSLazyColumn`. Never `Modifier.verticalScroll()` or Compose `LazyColumn`.

## Color

- Pick colors from the composable `scheme: ODSTheme` parameter, not hardcoded hex and not raw tokens when `scheme` is passed.
- Wrap with `ODSColorModel(hexColor = scheme.xxx)`. For `ODSIcon` tint use `scheme.xxx.getColor()`.

## Buttons, type, spacing

- `ODSButton` defaults to `ODSButtonSize.SMALL` unless the user says otherwise.
- Max text size is 16sp. Use `ODSTextStyles` with Funnel Sans (`bodyM*`, `bodyS*`, `microcopy*` only). No `title*`, `subtitle`, `bodyL`, or `display`.
- Padding, gaps, and radii: `ODSVariables` only. Never raw `16.dp` / `8.dp` for spacing.
